       scrollWidth past the viewport, so testing scrollWidth while they are
       still attached makes a padded row look like a real scroller and wipes
       the blanks again on the next resize. Detaching them first means the
       decision always reflects the true content width, which also lets the
       count self-correct when the window is resized. */
